      "writtenOn": "2024-02-26T17:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Typically reason holds PANIC_SW_* and info holds arbitrary context specific info (e.g. PC or assert line number). Exception is sometimes used to hold the task/thread id. This isn\u0027t ideal, but there is existing infrastructure that handles this form. So I\u0027d suggest something like: \npanic_set_reason(PANIC_SW_ZEPHYR_FATAL_ERROR, reason, task_get_current())",
      "revId": "1cebc9ef4aa8274bf839a4858b4af1d0597e8111",
